			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Refactor CHANGELOG entries to prose format\n\nConvert existing CHANGELOG version entries (v2.0 through v0.0) from bullet-point style to flowing narrative paragraphs. Each version section now reads as cohesive prose describing the quarter's accomplishments rather than disjointed bullet lists.\n\nThis improves changelog readability and provides a more engaging historical record of the project's evolution while maintaining full coverage of all features and milestones.",
			"SHA": "99c20dd13e2e46045e22c666370f2d8b1baaa62c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T04:58:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				102,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Update CHANGELOG to v2.2 and sync Element submodule\n\nUpdate the monorepo CHANGELOG with comprehensive v2.2 release notes covering the bundled-electron correctness pass: IPC reliability fixes (benign-404 classifier, URI parsing, path security, Promise-probe reduction), file-watching/reading/search fixes, workbench accessor transforms, and terminal channel-event bridging. Also sync Element submodule to 8273c12, bringing in:\n\n1. Output: ChannelEventBridge for terminal PTY events (localPty.onProcessData/exit routing through sky:// events)\n2. Sky: Search result format migration to VS Code ≥1.92 schema (previewText, rangeLocations)\n3. Cocoon: Downstream sync\n\nImpact: Terminals now render properly. Search panel displays results (was showing 0 despite matches).",
			"SHA": "76990ba463f1d3f196e15f785ee748a51f035ae5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T04:34:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				102,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Cocoon and Sky submodules\n\nUpdate Cocoon to d3408e6f8ffafedcf209a780133a8176bf0d9972 and Sky to b8a380955bb3217237de5df8129e2cadee710b52, bringing in the latest downstream improvements. This synchronization pulls in recent changes from both component repositories.",
			"SHA": "66fa9d3118502e31c35d8b267cd2c5b1b07d8b2d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T04:22:12Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				102,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Add terminal output buffering for late-listener replay\n\nMulti-component synchronization addressing the PTY reader vs SkyBridge listener race condition:\n\n1. Mountain: Add per-terminal output buffering - `AppendTerminalOutput()` captures PTY bytes into a 64KB bounded buffer (keeps most recent suffix to preserve the prompt), `DrainTerminalOutputBuffer()` retrieves buffered data, `RemoveTerminalOutputBuffer()` cleans up on exit. Extend `sky:replay-events` to emit `sky://terminal/create` for each active terminal AND replay any buffered `sky://terminal/data` bytes.\n\n2. Sky: Extend replay-events log with terminal visibility - Add `terminals?: number` and `terminalDataBytes?: number` to the type definition and include them in the log summary alongside tree-views, SCM providers, and commands. This provides visibility into terminal sessions active during early boot.\n\nThe race: In bundled-electron profile, the shell's first prompt fires ~50ms after `spawn_command` while Sky's bundle still parses for ~1500ms. Without buffering, zsh MOTD, direnv exports, fish greetings are silently dropped.\n\nImpact: Terminal output is now preserved and replayed for late listeners, completing the replay system for all three major feature areas: tree-views, SCM providers, and terminals.",
			"SHA": "93269905429d9f3e84d6640f85d2bd7290acd572"
		}
	],
